<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

use Illuminate\Database\Migrations\Migration;
use Illuminate\Database\Schema\Blueprint;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\DB;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Schema;

return new class extends Migration
{
    public function up(): void
    {
        Schema::create('users', function (Blueprint $table) {
            $table->id();
            $table->string('nombre', 120);
            $table->string('email', 150)->unique();
            $table->timestamp('email_verified_at')->nullable();
            $table->string('password');
            $table->enum('rol', ['administrador', 'operador', 'visualizador'])->default('visualizador')->index();
            $table->boolean('activo')->default(true);
            $table->rememberToken();
            $table->timestamps();
            $table->softDeletes();
        });

        // Un solo administrador activo: índice único parcial (PostgreSQL).
        DB::statement(
            "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX users_unico_administrador ON users (rol) WHERE rol = 'administrador' AND deleted_at IS NULL"
        );

        Schema::create('password_reset_tokens', ...);
        Schema::create('sessions', ...);
    }
    public function down(): void { Schema::dropIfExists('sessions'); ... }
};
```

Note: `$table->enum(...)->index()` — Laravel supports index on column. Good.

Recetas:

```php
Schema::create('recetas', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->foreignId('user_id')->constrained('users')->restrictOnDelete()->cascadeOnUpdate();
    $table->string('nombre', 150);
    $table->enum('tipo_producto', ['liquido', 'barra']);
    $table->enum('ingrediente_base', ['aceite', 'agua', 'sosa']);
    $table->decimal('peso', 10, 2)->comment('Peso del ingrediente base en gramos');
    $table->string('tipo_aceite', 80)->nullable();
    $table->jsonb('calculos')->comment('Proporciones calculadas por ingrediente');
    $table->jsonb('aditivos')->nullable();
    $table->timestamps();
    $table->index(['user_id', 'created_at']);
    $table->index('ingrediente_base');
});
```

Add CHECK peso > 0. Use DB::statement ALTER TABLE? Or Laravel has `$table->check()`? Not in core. Postgres supports CHECK inline; adding via raw statement in up() is fine, but on SQLite tests would break. We target PG strictly. I'll add CHECKs with DB::statement for key invariants (peso > 0, temperatura range, cantidad not null one-of). Keep count moderate (3), all in migrations after create.

Careful: `DB::statement` works only on Postgres/SQLite with ALTER ADD CONSTRAINT — SQLite doesn't support ADD CONSTRAINT. Tests using sqlite in-memory would fail. Hmm, phpunit.xml default uses sqlite :memory: in Laravel 12? Laravel 12 phpunit.xml has DB_CONNECTION=sqlite. If tests run, migrations with Postgres-specific DDL break. Options: guard with driver check:

```php
if (DB::getDriverName() === 'pgsql') { DB::statement(...); }
```

That's pragmatic and keeps tests runnable. But partial unique index for admin is also PG-specific — guard it too, else SQLite lacks it (and CHECK constraints can be inline there but skip).

Hmm, but silently skipping constraints on SQLite for tests is acceptable; production is PG. Alternatively I could just configure tests to use pgsql. Simpler and honest: guard with driver check and document. Actually for the admin uniqueness, I could enforce in app layer too (Rule). Fine.

But wait: `jsonb` column type is PG-specific! On SQLite, `jsonb` isn't a type → Laravel's SQLite grammar maps jsonb? Illuminate\Support\Facades\Schema grammar for SQLite: `typeJsonb` isn't defined... Actually Laravel 11+ added jsonb for Postgres; SQLite grammar has `typeJson` mapping. `$table->jsonb()` on SQLite → error "Unknown column type jsonb"? Laravel's SQLiteGrammar has typeJsonb? Hmm. In Laravel 11/12, `jsonb` is supported by Postgres and MySQL (alias json). SQLiteGrammar defines `typeJsonb`? I believe Laravel added `jsonb` to SQLite as `text`? Not sure.

Since target is strictly PostgreSQL, and tests can be configured to PG later, I'll not over-guard. But a broken `php artisan test` on the default sqlite config is a real papercut. Cleanest: set phpunit.xml DB_CONNECTION=pgsql? Then tests need a test DB. Hmm.

