content.text:
Now write User model, factory, and the other 9 models.

User model: relations typed with HasMany. Use `Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Relations\HasMany`. Add SoftDeletes.

Add helper `esAdministrador(): bool`, `puedeControlarMaquina()`, etc. Also `scopeActivos`. Also cast 'rol' => Rol::class.

Add `#[\Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Casts\Attribute]`? not needed.

For login with soft deletes, fine.

Careful: DB has `nombre` not `name`. Also the Authenticatable uses `email`. Good.

Write User:

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Models;

use App\Enums\Rol;
use Database\Factories\UserFactory;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Factories\HasFactory;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Relations\HasMany;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\SoftDeletes;
use Illuminate\Foundation\Auth\User as Authenticatable;
use Illuminate\Notifications\Notifiable;

class User extends Authenticatable
{
    use HasFactory, Notifiable, SoftDeletes;

    protected $fillable = ['nombre','email','password','rol','activo'];

    protected $hidden = ['password','remember_token'];

    protected function casts(): array
    {
        return [
            'email_verified_at' => 'datetime',
            'password' => 'hashed',
            'rol' => Rol::class,
            'activo' => 'boolean',
