Blade compile error at line 242: "Unclosed '[' does not match ')'" — that's the `@json(collect($componentesPanel)->mapWithKeys(fn ($c) => [$c['clave'] => [...]]))`.

Blade's `@json` with brackets/arrow functions confuses the compiler's parser because `@json(` parsing counts parentheses; the arrow fn with `=> [`... and nested `$c['clave']`? Actually error mentions '[' unclosed — the Blade parser handles `@json(...)` by finding matching parens; brackets inside are fine... Hmm.

Simplest fix: compute the array in PHP before the script block:

```blade
@php
    $accionesJs = collect($componentesPanel)->mapWithKeys(fn ($c) => [$c['clave'] => [
        'on' => $c['encender'], 'off' => $c['apagar'], 'pwm' => $c['pwm'],
    ]])->all();
@endphp
...
const acciones = @json($accionesJs);
```

That avoids complex inline expression inside @json. Let me edit.

Also fix the daily-programación logic (estaVencida): skip if created_at >= today's scheduled time.

Let me apply both.

For Programacion::estaVencida:
```php
if ($this->hora !== null) {
    $hoy = $ahora->copy()->setTimeFromTimeString((string) $this->hora);

    if ($hoy->gt($ahora)) return false;               // aún no llega la hora
    if ($this->created_at !== null && $this->created_at->gte($hoy)) return false; // creada después de la hora de hoy: empieza mañana
    return $this->ultima_ejecucion === null || ! $this->ultima_ejecucion->isSameDay($ahora);
}
```

Wait: created_at gte $hoy — created 23:40, hoy 08:30 → created_at > hoy → return false. Good.
If created at 07:00 for 08:30 → created < hoy, hora passed at 08:30 → executes. Good.

Edge: created at 08:30:05 for 08:30 → created >= hoy (08:30:00) → won't run today. Slight edge, acceptable (would run tomorrow). Better to compare with a small tolerance? Keep simple.

Also for one-shot retardo: `ultima_ejecucion === null && ejecutar_en <= ahora` — fine.

Let me apply edits.

